{
  "_comment": "Model IDs are OpenRouter slugs. Check them with `node router.mjs check` (needs network access to openrouter.ai) and edit freely. Each list is tried in order; openrouter/auto is always the last fallback. Refreshed from OpenRouter's catalog on 2026-09-25; \"open\" means the weights are published (the catalog lists a Hugging Face ID). \"decider\" answers Jev's questions while no Jev key is set (ROUTER_DECIDER_MODEL overrides it); \"open\" is used with --open. \"free\" holds zero-cost models (OpenRouter ':free' variants, openrouter/free) used when the key is out of credit (HTTP 402) or with --free; free models are rate-limited (20/min, 50/day, or 1000/day once $10 of credit has been bought). \"local\" is optional: --local builds each route from the pulled Ollama models, ranked by size (largest first for code, reasoning, long_context and writing; mid-size for general; smallest of at least 1B for quick); a list of Ollama model names under a category overrides that (a name without a tag matches any pulled tag of it).",
  "owned": {
    "_comment": "Providers the owner already pays for by subscription (owner, 2026-09-26: a ChatGPT plan, a Gemini Enterprise seat and a Claude plan). Paid routes never send these providers' models, nor openrouter/auto, to OpenRouter; their work goes to the subscription's own agent (Codex, Gemini CLI, Claude Code). ROUTER_OWNED overrides this list (\"none\" turns it off); --allow-owned overrides it for one call. Free models are left alone.",
    "families": [
      "openai",
      "google",
      "anthropic"
    ]
  },
  "agents": {
    "_comment": "The subscription agents that do an owned family's work on the owner's own sign-in, run as command-line tools. Used by the default order (local, then these, then free, then paid) when the route Jev picked names a model of that family; a tool that is not installed is skipped. {prompt} is replaced by the prompt (passed as one argument, never through a shell). The tool uses its own default model; the route only decides which subscription to use.",
    "anthropic": {
      "command": "claude",
      "args": [
        "-p",
        "{prompt}", "--model", "{model}"
      ]
    },
    "google": {
      "command": "gemini",
      "args": [
        "-p",
        "{prompt}"
      ]
    },
    "openai": {
      "command": "codex",
      "args": [
        "exec",
        "{prompt}"
      ]
    }
  },
